<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13244] Transaction commit completes successfully if partition is lost on commit phase</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13244</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Reproducer is attached.&lt;br/&gt;
Steps:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Run startNode()&lt;br/&gt;
2) Run poorTransaction() in a separate JVM&lt;br/&gt;
3) Hang first node in GridCacheMapEntry#innerSet with a breakpoint&lt;br/&gt;
4) kill -9 first node while hanging on breakpoint&lt;br/&gt;
5) Result: tx.commit() succeeds, data is commited in partition 1 and not commited in partition 2&lt;/p&gt;</description>
